  "groundzero.holo_projector.nothing": "No unfinished structure in range",
  "groundzero.holo_projector.tooltip": "Hold near an unfinished multiblock to project it. Use to step through its layers.",
  "groundzero.info.chemical_plant": "Chemical Plant (2x2x2): put the controller down, then add Machine Casing beside it and behind it, an Item Port in the far corner of that bottom layer, and four Reactor Glass on top. Right-click the controller, or hold a Holo-Projector, to see where each block goes (sneak-right-click opens it before it is finished). Feed items through the Item Port or the controller's open faces and pipe fluids in (a Water Pump supplies water). Right-click with a bucket or canister to pour it in, sneak-right-click with an empty one to draw off the product.",
  "groundzero.info.die": "Goes in the Industrial Press die slot and picks what the press makes. Dies are never used up.",
  "groundzero.info.fluid_pipe": "Fluid pipes carry what machines push out of faces with auto-eject and fluids switched on, sharing it between every tank the pipe run touches. Pipes hold nothing themselves, so breaking one never spills. Up to 2,000 mB per tick per run.",
  "groundzero.info.fluid_tank": "Each Fluid Tank holds 16,000 mB. Touching tanks join into one when together they fill a box with a square base up to 3x3 and up to 5 high (720,000 mB). Pipes fill it from any side; it lets liquids out of its bottom (gases out of its top) into whatever is there.",
  "groundzero.info.fluids": "Chemical fluids live in machine tanks, pipes, canisters and (liquids only) buckets. Spilled acids burn, napalm ignites and liquid oxygen or nitrogen freeze anything standing in them.",
  "groundzero.info.membrane": "Goes in the Cryogenic Condenser's membrane slot and picks which gas it liquefies. Membranes are never used up.",
  "groundzero.info.sides": "Every machine has a side-configuration tab (the wrench on the right of its screen): choose which faces accept items, give out products and connect to power, and switch on auto-eject.",
  "groundzero.info.water_pump": "Place on a water source block and power it: it draws 50 mB of water a tick (the source is never used up) and pushes it into pipes, tanks and machines on every side with fluids switched on.",
